--- the base brick (what runs today, plus the session and log settings)
ok   sessions: 2h idle, 12h in all
ok   the local login form is NOT hidden
ok   the role mapping is permissive: strict false and a Viewer fallback
ok   every HTTP request is logged, as JSON
ok   SSO still creates the user at first login
ok   the server root_url and the database survive the section move
--- the SSO-only overlay (off by default)
ok   it hides the local login form
ok   it keeps the session lifetimes
ok   the role mapping is strict
ok   grafana-admin gives Admin
ok   grafana-viewer gives Viewer
ok   both: Admin wins
ok   any other role gives nothing (strict then denies)
ok   no roles claim at all gives nothing
ok   nothing else differs between the base and the overlay
--- the chart rendered with each (grafana.ini as Grafana will read it)
ok   base: [auth] carries the lifetimes
ok   base: [log.console] format = json and router_logging = true
ok   base: disable_login_form is absent
ok   base: role_attribute_strict = false
ok   only: [auth] carries the lifetimes
ok   only: [log.console] format = json and router_logging = true
ok   only: disable_login_form is set
ok   only: role_attribute_strict = true
